      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹70.47 (vs ₹73.09 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹70.47 (down from ₹73.09 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹41.5b (up 14% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹3.48b (down 3.4% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 8.4% (down from 9.9% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue is forecast to grow 6.8% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Chemicals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 14% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 27% per year, which means it is tracking significantly ahead of earnings growth.",
